<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chronicle of the Morea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chronicle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Morea</a> is a fourteenth-century history of the Frankish Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a> in the Peloponnese, surviving in Greek, French, Aragonese and Italian versions. It covers the conquest after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>, the reigns of the Villehardouin princes and the later history of the principality. It is a main source for Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and its baronies and for local peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melingoi">Melingoi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-the-morea.jpg" alt="Chronicle of the Morea" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Text_from_the_Chronicle_of_Morea.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
